    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 267 tests, 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the owner initials feature by following the existing `displayName` derived-field pattern (this project computes such fields in the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, not in a function step).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` field to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` includes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `initials` on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n   This produces the upper-cased, dot-separated initials with trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nBecause the `RespondWithOwnerCreated` step already maps the entity through `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto`, the new field flows into the create response automatically \u2014 no new function class or YAML step was needed.\n\nThe new `Cp07Tests.coreInitials` passes (`J.S.`), along with all pre-existing tests including `Cp06` (displayName).",
